<title>FRANCE: OECD forecasts for the Netherlands.</title>
<headline>OECD forecasts for the Netherlands.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development (OECD) published the following forecasts for the Dutch economy in its June Economic Outlook.</p>
<p>    OECD FORECAST NETHERLANDS	1998   1997   1996   1995</p>
<p>    Gross domestic product	    3.2    3.0    2.7    2.1</p>
<p>    Private consumption		 2.3    2.3    2.9    2.1</p>
<p>    Government consumption	    2.3    2.3    0.5    0.6</p>
<p>    Gross fixed investment	    2.6    4.4    5.5    6.7</p>
<p>    Final domestic demand	     2.4    2.8    3.1    2.8</p>
<p>    Exports goods and services	6.8    5.6    4.0    6.9</p>
<p>    Imports goods and services	6.0    5.6    5.8    7.7</p>
<p>    GDP price deflator		  2.1    1.9    1.4    1.5</p>
<p>    Private consumption deflator    1.9    1.8    1.8    0.9</p>
<p>    Unemployment rate		   5.6    6.2    6.7    7.1</p>
<p>    Household saving ratio	    0.6    0.5    1.3    2.0</p>
<p>    Current account balance	   4.9    4.4    4.7    5.0</p>
<p>NOTES -- Figures show real percentage changes with following exceptions: unemployment is expressed as percentage of labour force; savings ratio as percentage of disposable income; current account balance as percentage of GDP.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
